From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:34:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] net: ipa: add IPA v4.1 support (SM8150)

SM8150 has IPA v4.1 with GSI 2.0. Add its configuration data and register set:
- ipa_data-v4.1.c: endpoints, resource limits, memory layout and power data from the
  downstream SM8150 tables (IPA_4_1), the memory layout = v3.5.1's plus the v4.0 stats regions;
- ipa_reg-v4.1.c: the v4.2 register set plus what v4.2 dropped and v4.1 still has (hashed
  filter/route tables, four resource groups, ENDP_INIT_CTRL);
- GSI registers = gsi_reg-v4.0.c (GSI 2.0, as v4.2), and the qcom,sm8150-ipa compatible.

Tested on a Surface Duo (SM8150): the driver loads the GSI firmware, completes setup with the
modem (modem starting/running events, QMI init), creates rmnet_ipa0 and stays up with the
modem running.

This patch was written by Claude (Anthropic's AI assistant) under the direction of Bryson, who reviewed and
tested it on a Surface Duo.

Signed-off-by: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
